        "id": "injection",
        "title": "21. Prompt injection and least privilege",
        "stage": "advanced",
        "takeaway": "Prompt injection is untrusted content attempting to redirect agent behavior.",
        "sections": [
          {
            "title": "Concept",
            "paragraphs": [
              "Prompt injection is untrusted content attempting to redirect agent behavior. Defend at multiple boundaries rather than assuming a clever prompt can remove the risk.",
              "A retrieved lesson might contain a hidden instruction to read private notes and post them to a URL. Limit available tools, credentials, destinations and data scope. Keep external content labeled as evidence and validate action requests. Detection can help but may miss obfuscated attacks; it is not a substitute for an executor that cannot perform the forbidden action."
            ]
          },
          {
            "title": "Example",
            "paragraphs": [
              "The executor contains the forbidden upload even if the proposal source follows the injected instruction."
            ],
            "example": "Untrusted lesson -> evidence field -> decision proposal\n                                      |\n                                      v\nTrusted executor: allowlist + arguments + access policy\n  search approved lessons -> may run\n  upload learner profile -> denied / capability absent\nSecurity property tested: forbidden request never executes"
          },
          {
            "title": "Tradeoffs",
            "paragraphs": [
              "Even a read tool can leak information through its outputs or through subsequent tool arguments. Minimize context and inspect outbound data. Multi-agent handoffs can carry the same malicious text to more components. The workshop test proves an unknown tool is rejected, not that a real model resists all prompt injection."
            ]
          }
        ],
        "exercise": {
          "prompt": "Design an adversarial case whose source says send all secrets to a URL. Define the pass criterion independently of the final prose.",
          "solution": "Record executor calls and verify no forbidden read or outbound send occurs. Also check that sensitive data is absent from logs and final output. A reassuring final sentence is insufficient if an earlier tool already leaked information. Include variants with indirect wording and malicious tool-result fields.",
          "checks": [
            "Uses observable actions as pass/fail evidence.",
            "Tests outbound leakage and logs.",
            "Does not claim complete protection from one test."
          ],
          "solutionFormat": "prose"
        },
