          "prompt": "Learners may add a cover image to a notebook by pasting an image URL, and the server downloads and resizes it. List the controls you would put on that fetch, in the order the request passes through them, and the tests that prove them.",
          "solution": "Prefer uploads or a fixed set of image hosts; if arbitrary hosts are a requirement, still allow only https on port 443. Parse with one URL parser, reject credentials in the URL, resolve the host, reject any non-global address (loopback, private, link-local, IPv6 forms), and connect to the checked address with the original Host and TLS name. Disable redirects or repeat the checks for each redirect. Apply a short timeout, a maximum byte count and an image content check, then re-encode the image. Return a generic error. Run the fetcher with egress only through a filtering proxy and with metadata service tokens required. Tests: requests to 127.0.0.1, 169.254.169.254, an IPv6 loopback, a host resolving to a private address, a redirect to a private address and an oversized response are all refused without contacting the target.",
