          "prompt": "Write answer(values, queries) that returns sum(values[i:j]) for each (i, j) query using one prefix array. Check it against direct sums for 500 random half-open ranges over 100 values that include negatives, including empty ranges, then print the answers for [30, 0, 45, 15] with queries (0, 4), (1, 3) and (2, 2).",
          "solution": "import random\nfrom itertools import accumulate\n\ndef answer(values, queries):\n    prefix = [0, *accumulate(values)]\n    return [prefix[j] - prefix[i] for i, j in queries]\n\nrng = random.Random(5)\nvalues = [rng.randint(-50, 50) for _ in range(100)]\nqueries = [tuple(sorted((rng.randint(0, 100), rng.randint(0, 100)))) for _ in range(500)]\nassert answer(values, queries) == [sum(values[i:j]) for i, j in queries]\nprint(answer([30, 0, 45, 15], [(0, 4), (1, 3), (2, 2)]))",
